<title>UK: UK windfall tax to cover 3 bln stg job plan-Labour.</title>
<headline>UK windfall tax to cover 3 bln stg job plan-Labour.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The opposition Labour party's economics spokesman Gordon Brown said on Thursday his proposed windfall tax will cover the cost of a jobs programme costing three billion pounds over the life of the next parliament.</p>
<p>Brown declined to single out which companies would be covered. He also declined to say the total amount the windfall tax on privatised would raise.</p>
<p>But he added: &quot;The employment programme... will cost three billion pounds I believe that without naming a figure the windfall levy... that figure of three billion pounds can be comfortably financed by the windfall levy in government.&quot; -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7768</p>
</text>
